msgid "Editing the code with VSCode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:7
#: e600cf8567de4fa5a4a99b5aa2beb8e7
msgid "VSCode is free and available on all desktop platforms: Windows, Linux, MacOS. VSCode can be downloaded from `here <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:9
#: 32801cb630e24afc9c591e3a29e56f25
msgid "It bundles all tools need to build ArduPilot: C/C++ support, python support, git support, and :ref:`debugging support <debugging-with-gdb-using-vscode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:11
#: 7bd7910298e74be7a03e5584c99436b0
msgid "For Windows 10 users, the Remote - WSL extension lets you use the Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) as your full-time development environment right from VS Code: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/tutorials/wsl-vscode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:13
#: e3c22c41cd264facba818dcf8d05bda8
msgid "For users that might want to collaborate on code using VSCode, `VSCode provides a Live Share utility <https://code.visualstudio.com/learn/collaboration/live-share>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:17
#: 71c404a364354acea89ff05d2db3734b
msgid "ArduPilot VSCode Extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-the-code-with-vscode.rst:19
#: 2439653bc30d49f8b0a6a897814cccff
msgid "There is an official ArduPilot VSCode extension that creates tasks on demand. The marketplace page for the extension is `here <https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ardupilot-org.ardupilot-devenv>`__. A video demonstrating using the extension is `here <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQMzclWC6u0>`__."
